   "img": "systems/arneyan/assets/icons/spell-magic-portal.svg",
   "system": {
    "description": "<p>Cast as a spell: duplicates any spell of 8th level or lower, using your caster level and spell DC and ignoring its material components; the duplicated spell's own save applies.</p><ul><li>It cannot return the dead; use the Ritual.</li><li>Cast as a Ritual (no slot; takes <strong>1 hour</strong>; consumes 2,500 gp of components; you gain 2 levels of Exhaustion): shape reality by choosing one effect: raise one attribute of one creature by 1 permanently (once per creature); return a dead creature to life as True Resurrection, with no body or time limit needed (plus 25,000 gp of diamond dust); end any curse, disease, affliction, attribute loss or Exhaustion; free a creature from Imprisonment, Temporal Stasis, Maze or Trap the Soul; create one nonmagical object worth up to 2,500 gp; or transport up to 8 creatures anywhere on any plane.</li><li>Any other effect must be approved by the GM before the ritual begins; it cannot kill a creature outright or grant levels, and the GM names its cost up front.</li></ul><p class=\"arn-note\"><strong>Costly component:</strong> see Rare Spell Components in the Shopkeeper's Catalogue.</p><p class=\"arn-note\"><strong>Classes:</strong> Wizard</p>",
